; The elevator intro, whole. Local metres; the car's doorway faces -Z, so the
; placement in a level is a position and a yaw and nothing else.
;
; POSES ARE IN THIS SCENE'S SPACE, NOT THE LEVEL'S. Every camera pose in
; elevator_intro_knobs.gd and every track path in the generated clip is relative
; to this root, which is why AnimationPlayer.root_node points three levels up at
; it rather than at the level. asteroid_level instances this at the mine mouth
; and the prototype instances it in a greybox shaft; the shot is identical in
; both because neither placement is in any of the numbers.
;
; NO WorldEnvironment. PlayerView writes fog into the level's shared one at
; _ready, and a second one arriving with the cutscene would repaint the level
; every time the intro loaded.

